{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hpb4upglnptjqb55affvgka3awaiqjhbqfykwwgxikgs6hsj2sxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_014fFHadmrCNs7rqhQ6ddphs","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"QglxjtWQDep2UafV2cHQ1a","description":"Read all text on Start Here and Foundations pages","code":"const out=[];for(const id of ['0:1','1:2']){const p=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(p);out.push('=== '+p.name);const walk=(n,d)=>{let s='  '.repeat(d)+n.type+' '+n.id+' \"'+n.name+'\" '+Math.round(n.x||0)+','+Math.round(n.y||0)+' '+Math.round(n.width||0)+'x'+Math.round(n.height||0);if(n.type==='TEXT')s+=' :: '+n.characters;out.push(s);if('children'in n&&d<6)n.children.forEach(c=>walk(c,d+1));};p.children.forEach(c=>walk(c,0));}return out.join('\\n');"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":969,"cache_read_input_tokens":7912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":969,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd6a2ae-4049-4f72-83c7-152b735f2752","uuid":"8237750d-23d7-4b00-bb40-e4abd35367ef","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:58:45.886Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_014fFHadmrCNs7rqhQ6ddphs","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014fFHadmrCNs7rqhQ6ddphs","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== 00 · Start Here 设计任务\nFRAME 4:2 \"Start Here · Brief\" 0,0 1440x2618\n  FRAME 4:3 \"Header\" 64,64 1312x145\n    TEXT 4:4 \"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" 0,0 182x19 :: LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\n    TEXT 4:5 \"ABM — developer portfolio\" 0,31 1312x52 :: ABM — developer portfolio\n    TEXT 4:6 \"Design a one-page portfolio for a full-stack software engineer: who they are, the tech they use, two projects, work experience and contact. Desktop web, 1440 wide, dark mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" 0,95 1312x50 :: Design a one-page portfolio for a full-stack software engineer: who they are, the tech they use, two projects, work experience and contact. Desktop web, 1440 wide, dark mode. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\n  FRAME 4:7 \"How to work\" 64,257 1312x227\n    TEXT 4:8 \"How to work\" 0,0 147x35 :: How to work\n    TEXT 4:9 \"1. Build exactly the 1 frame below, named exactly as listed. It is a single page (the navigation scrolls to sections), so there is no prototype to wire. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The two brand accents and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the signature logo, the avatar, the project images, the tech and social logos and the icons from 04 · Media. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" 0,51 1312x176 :: 1. Build exactly the 1 frame below, named exactly as listed. It is a single page (the navigation scrolls to sections), so there is no prototype to wire.\n2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in page order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions.\n3. The two brand accents and the typeface in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself, plus type scale, spacing, radii, elevation and the page grid, and apply them consistently.\n4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button. Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file.\n5. Use the signature logo, the avatar, the project images, the tech and social logos and the icons from 04 · Media.\n6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\n  FRAME 4:10 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 64,532 1312x645\n    TEXT 4:11 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 0,0 413x35 :: Frames · goals · must include · links\n    TEXT 4:12 \"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" 0,51 1312x22 :: Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\n    FRAME 4:13 \"Frame cards\" 0,89 1312x556\n      FRAME 4:14 \"01_Home\" 0,0 644x556\n        TEXT 4:15 \"01_Home\" 24,24 82x26 :: 01_Home\n        TEXT 4:16 \"Goal: Understand who the engineer is, see their work and get in touch.\" 24,60 596x20 :: Goal: Understand who the engineer is, see their work and get in touch.\n        TEXT 4:17 \"MUST INCLUDE\" 24,90 84x16 :: MUST INCLUDE\n        TEXT 4:18 \"• Contact: “Contact” · “Seasoned Full Stack Software Engineer with over 8 years of hands-on experience in designing and implementing robust, scalable, and innovative web solutions. Adept at leveraging a comprehensive skill set encompassing front-end and back-end technologies.” · “abm@example.com” (Icon_Mail) · Logo_Instagram · Logo_X · Logo_YouTube • Experience: “Experience” · 3 entries, each with a company initials mark, role and company, dates and description (see DATA) • Header: Logo_ABM · navigation Home / Projects / Experience / Contact · current: Home • Hero: Photo_Avatar · “I do code and make content about it!” · “I am a seasoned full-stack software engineer with over 8 years of professional experience, specializing in backend development. My expertise lies in crafting robust and scalable SaaS-based architectures on the Amazon AWS platform.” · “Get In Touch” · “Download CV” • Projects: “Projects” · 2 project cards, each with photo, “CLICK HERE TO VISIT”, title and open (Icon_Arrow_Up_Right): HTML TUTORIAL (Photo_Project_HTML) · CSS TUTORIAL (Photo_Project_CSS) • Tech stack: “EXPERIENCE WITH” · Logo_JavaScript · Logo_Nextjs · Logo_HTML5 · Logo_CSS3 · Logo_React\" 24,116 596x340 :: • Contact: “Contact” · “Seasoned Full Stack Software Engineer with over 8 years of hands-on experience in designing and implementing robust, scalable, and innovative web solutions. Adept at leveraging a comprehensive skill set encompassing front-end and back-end technologies.” · “abm@example.com” (Icon_Mail) · Logo_Instagram · Logo_X · Logo_YouTube\n• Experience: “Experience” · 3 entries, each with a company initials mark, role and company, dates and description (see DATA)\n• Header: Logo_ABM · navigation Home / Projects / Experience / Contact · current: Home\n• Hero: Photo_Avatar · “I do code and make content about it!” · “I am a seasoned full-stack software engineer with over 8 years of professional experience, specializing in backend development. My expertise lies in crafting robust and scalable SaaS-based architectures on the Amazon AWS platform.” · “Get In Touch” · “Download CV”\n• Projects: “Projects” · 2 project cards, each with photo, “CLICK HERE TO VISIT”, title and open (Icon_Arrow_Up_Right): HTML TUTORIAL (Photo_Project_HTML) · CSS TUTORIAL (Photo_Project_CSS)\n• Tech stack: “EXPERIENCE WITH” · Logo_JavaScript · Logo_Nextjs · Logo_HTML5 · Logo_CSS3 · Logo_React\n        TEXT 4:19 \"LINKS\" 24,466 33x16 :: LINKS\n        TEXT 4:20 \"Single-page task: no links between frames. Navigation items scroll to sections; every button and link is entry only.\" 24,492 596x40 :: Single-page task: no links between frames. Navigation items scroll to sections; every button and link is entry only.\n  FRAME 4:21 \"Navigation structure\" 64,1225 1312x117\n    TEXT 4:22 \"Navigation structure\" 0,0 242x35 :: Navigation structure\n    TEXT 4:23 \"• One frame. The header and the contact footer are part of it. • Home / Projects / Experience / Contact scroll to the matching section on the same page (no extra frames). • Entry only (no frame): Get In Touch, Download CV, project cards, email address, social logos.\" 0,51 1312x66 :: • One frame. The header and the contact footer are part of it.\n• Home / Projects / Experience / Contact scroll to the matching section on the same page (no extra frames).\n• Entry only (no frame): Get In Touch, Download CV, project cards, email address, social logos.\n  FRAME 4:24 \"Fixed data & copy\" 64,1390 1312x537\n    TEXT 4:25 \"Fixed data & copy\" 0,0 207x35 :: Fixed data & copy\n    TEXT 4:26 \"Use these values verbatim.\" 0,51 1312x22 :: Use these values verbatim.\n    FRAME 4:27 \"Data blocks\" 0,89 1312x448\n      FRAME 4:28 \"Experience (in order, newest first)\" 0,0 420x448\n        TEXT 4:29 \"Experience (in order, newest first)\" 20,20 233x20 :: Experience (in order, newest first)\n        TEXT 4:30 \"Lead Software Engineer at Searchlight · Nov 2019 – Present — “As a Lead Software Engineer at Se